# Security headers for Cloudflare Pages. This file is NOT active locally:
# Cloudflare Pages parses it only at deploy time. CSP is safe to add
# because all executable scripts moved to external same-origin files
# (theme.js, countdown.js, filters.js, playground.js); the only remaining
# <script> tags are application/ld+json data blocks, which are not executed.
# connect-src https: is required for the browser-only playground, which
# calls providers directly from the visitor's browser. No server proxy.
# img-src/media-src https: is required for provider-hosted generated
# images and videos displayed in the playground.
# CSP cannot be live-tested locally (no headers are served by `astro build`
# output alone); it takes effect only after a Cloudflare Pages deploy,
# and must be re-checked in the browser then for theme, countdown,
# filters, and playground before being treated as fully verified.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' https: data:; media-src 'self' https:; connect-src 'self' https:; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
